```mdl
verdict F-1.1: A Feed is an append log of ECHO objects.
  status: done
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.ts#Feed, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.ts#append]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo-client-e2e/src/feed.test.ts]
```

```mdl
verdict F-1.2: Branches work, but in the earlier form: foreign keys and item ids, not meta fields and block ids.
  status: diverged
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.ts#startBranch, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.ts#readBranch, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.ts#append]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.test.ts, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo-client-e2e/src/feed-branch.test.ts]
  note: |
    The code stores the branch in the `org.dxos.key.feed-branch` key, with the id of the first item as
    the branch id, and the fork point in the `org.dxos.key.feed-fork` key. The spec now puts both in
    `@meta.feed` [D-29], uses the block id of the base block as the branch id [D-27], and takes the fork
    point from the predecessor of the block [D-28].
```

