```mdl
verdict F-2.1: The index holds the main branch or all branches, and a branch scope filters before the limit. The time range is missing.
  status: partial
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.ts#IndexingOptions, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo-host/src/db-host/feed-data-source.ts#indexesAllBranches, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/index-core/src/indexes/entity-meta-index.ts#buildQueueBranchCondition, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Scope.ts#feed]
  tests: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/index-core/src/indexes/entity-meta-index.test.ts, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo-host/src/query/query-executor.test.ts, github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo-host/src/db-host/feed-data-source.test.ts]
  walkthrough:
    - IndexingOptions has a mode of all or main, and main is the default. github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo/src/Feed.ts#IndexingOptions
    - The indexer skips the blocks of a branch unless the mode is all. github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/echo-host/src/db-host/feed-data-source.ts#indexesAllBranches
    - Scope.feed takes branches, and the query puts the branch filter before the order and the limit. github:dxos/dxos/packages/core/echo/index-core/src/indexes/entity-meta-index.ts#buildQueueBranchCondition
  note: |
    A query can have a scope of a set of branches. The scope has no time range (`after`, `before`)
    yet.
```

```mdl
verdict F-2.2: The feed store has a head for each namespace, not for each branch.
