    The feed store gives an answer for a caught-up cursor, and it does not read blocks for this
    answer. It moves a head for each namespace (feed-store tests "answers a caught-up cursor…" and
    "moves the head of the namespace…"). No call gives the branches whose heads changed since a cursor.
